  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `wall_lean` (new, `crates/motion/src/machining2d/chamfer_ride.rs`) gives the plan move of an upright wall in the operation frame. With no frame or an upright frame, the move is zero. With the tool axis in the world XY plane, it gives `None`.\n- `ride_loops` takes this move as a new argument. The app caller (`material_source.rs`) computes it from the frame and the chamfer depth.\n- `leans` accepts only this move. It does not read the move from the section centroids any more. The `centroid` helper is removed.\n- `partly_bevelled` cuts each top segment at the foot of each wall vertex inside it. Then it judges each piece as before.\n- The unit tests move to `chamfer_ride_tests.rs`, so that the source file stays under 400 lines.\n- `docs/decisions/2936-chamfer-leaning-wall.md`: the sentence \"Thus the new test cannot hide a case of #2887\" is corrected.\n- New decision file: `docs/decisions/2944-chamfer-lean-frame.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe part has a 1 mm bevel on the -X side and a 1 mm undercut lip on the +X side. The top section `[-29,31] x [-20,20]` is the wall section `[-30,30] x [-20,20]` moved 1 mm in X. The old `leans` found this move from the centroids and skipped the #2887 refusal.\n\nA second cause showed in the test. Each Y side of the top section is one segment from X-29 to X31. Its X31 end is off the wall. The old judgement read the whole segment as bevelled. Thus no segment was sharp, and the refusal did not occur even without the lean exemption. The cut at X30 now gives a 59 mm sharp piece and a 1 mm lip piece.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Pin: `machining2d::chamfer_ride::tests::an_upright_bevel_beside_an_equal_undercut_lip_still_refuses`. Red on unchanged code (the part rode the wall `[-30,30]` all round). Green with the fix.\n- New: `the_wall_lean_is_the_frames_own` (no frame, upright, 10 degree tilt, horizontal axis).\n- The box under a 10 degree tilt (#2936) still generates: `framed_stock_chamfer_live_refusal_keeps_hint_without_local_move_number` (`stock_source_holes`) passes.\n- Mutations:\n  - Lean sign flipped in `wall_lean`: `framed_stock_chamfer_live_refusal_keeps_hint_without_local_move_number` red (partly-bevelled refusal). The sign is checked end to end.\n  - No segment pieces: the pin red.\n  - Lean read off the sections again: the pin red.\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`): 136 steps, 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A real STEP model of the bevel-and-lip plate. The pin uses hand-built sections.\n- A tilted frame with a part that has true draft walls. It is read as before #2936 (the safe reading).\n- Heavy lanes were not run.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #2836 and #2714 touch `crates/app/src/operation/material_source.rs`, in a different match arm (near line 237). Whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nChangelog: A no-pick 2D Chamfer on a part with a bevel on one side and an equal undercut lip on the other side is refused by name again, and is not cut all round.\n\nFixes #2944\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
